import ../../../examples/snake/application.dl

[menu surface] means: UI node 22 with "menu" colored "" sized 0 by 0 bordered 0 containing no UI children acting no UI action
[playing surface] means: UI node 22 with "playing" colored "" sized 0 by 0 bordered 0 containing no UI children acting no UI action
[settings surface] means: UI node 22 with "settings" colored "" sized 0 by 0 bordered 0 containing no UI children acting no UI action

set game to a new snake session
set instance to an instance of menu surface with state (the address of game)
set instance's page to menu surface
set view to a new UI view
set view's instance to the address of instance
set view's input kind to 3
set view's key press to 265
read snake input from (the address of view)
require condition ((view's input handled = false) and (view's key press = 265)) reporting "The menu stole direction keys from its controls."
set instance's page to settings surface
read snake input from (the address of view)
require condition (view's input handled = false) reporting "Settings stole direction keys from its controls."
set instance's page to playing surface
begin a run in (the address of game)
set view's input kind to 9
read snake input from (the address of view)
require condition ((view's input handled) and (game's direction = 1)) reporting "A repeated direction key turned the snake or leaked its default."
set view's input kind to 3
set view's key press to 265
read snake input from (the address of view)
require condition ((view's input handled) and (game's direction = 0)) reporting "A fresh direction key did not turn and claim its event."
close the address of instance
close the address of game
print line "Snake claims fresh and repeated direction keys only on the playing surface, and turns only on a fresh press."
